# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-5, R-14). L §3.1 A day key where a date is expected: "Where a date is expected (an operand of a
# comparison, min or max with a date, an if branch whose other branch is a date, a date argument), a key of a day index
# may stand, and means start_of(k): a day has one date. A day index is days or a range of day periods without by n
# (§4.1). A key of a month or a year index, or of a day range by n, doesn't convert ...: it is written, and the mixed form
# stays refused (LOAD-UNIT)".
# min and max of a day key and a date (the keys and cutoff carried).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input cutoff: date
input flag: bool
def lo[d in days]: date = min(d, cutoff) at cutoff
def hi[d in days]: date = max(cutoff, d) at cutoff
ask q: lo[2026-03-09], lo[2026-03-12], hi[2026-03-12]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cutoff = 2026-03-10
  flag = true
=== expect
q: (2026-03-09, 2026-03-10, 2026-03-12)
  cut 2026-01-01
warning: WARN-UNREAD input flag is read by nothing
